[{"round": 1, "proposal": {"experiment_id": "za_four_tile_reuse", "recommendation": "Propose changing only the full-512 compute traversal in `Llibxsmm_440` and its two K loops. The current path computes two 32-row output halves for each 32-column B panel, then advances B; ZA0\u2013ZA3 hold the four 32\u00d732 output tiles. Test reversing the outer traversal: for each 32-row A panel, visit all sixteen 32-column B panels before moving to the next A panel. Keep four ZA tiles, FP32 FMOPA order, existing packed-A layout, and each panel\u2019s stores. Update B/C starting pointers, increments, and loop resets together so each tile uses the same operands and writes the same disjoint output region. Hypothesis: keeping one packed A panel active across more B panels may improve reuse; benefit is unknown. This is distinct from the tested 64\u00d732 traversal, but requires careful pointer and accumulator remapping. Check that no output tile is skipped or written twice, all K steps and tails remain correct, scratch accesses stay within allocation, SME enters/exits correctly, and the full GEMM passes the fixed tolerance for n=512 and general sizes including n<=0. Then compare fresh repeated paired controls with unchanged power settings; report spread and do not attribute any noisy gain to this reuse mechanism alone.", "risks": "Traversal reversal may increase B or C address work, disrupt the generated kernel\u2019s intended access pattern, or remap FMOPA operands to the wrong ZA tile. The supplied evidence does not establish a cache bottleneck or predict a speedup. Keep the original full-kernel path available for comparison; do not claim an improvement before paired gates pass."}, "experiment_id": "za_four_tile_reuse", "status": "proposed", "source_hash": "367df33b6712e12a758295c494b013fdd2f5aaa034bf82488cf8754f349a82a0"}, {"round": 1, "proposal": {"experiment_id": "b_panel_layout", "recommendation": "Propose a distinct B-layout experiment in the full512 kernel: keep the existing 64-row output macroblock and one SME call, but pack each 32-column B panel from row-major B[k*512+j] into a contiguous K-major panel inside the timed call. Update the full512 SME consumer\u2019s B pointer and K stride to read that panel; keep the A pack, FP32 FMOPA order, C stores, ABI, fallback, and license unchanged. This tests whether contiguous panel access offsets the extra B packing work. It is a hypothesis, not a measured improvement. Specify exact panel indexing and pointer rewinds before implementation; do not combine it with the supplied panel32 helper or change the fixed benchmark.", "risks": "Packing adds timed loads and stores and may cost more than it saves. The current SME loop expects two 32-column B vectors per K step; the new layout must preserve both vectors, all 512 K values, and correct panel transitions. Incorrect strides or rewinds could corrupt results. Check full GEMM at n=512 and general sizes, tails, and n<=0 against the 0.002 tolerance; confirm only FP32 arithmetic and no external libraries. Then use fresh paired controls under unchanged power settings and the fixed promotion gates. No speedup or target attainment is established."}, "experiment_id": "b_panel_layout", "status": "proposed", "source_hash": "f21047135d3ab2f71b92c91cfca9546b101d4382563330f4bb375b2f94557a36"}, {"round": 1, "proposal": {"experiment_id": "loop_order", "recommendation": "Propose an n=512 loop-order variant that interchanges the existing full-kernel outer traversal from 64-row blocks with 32-column panels to 32-column panels with 64-row blocks. In the `Llibxsmm_64`/`Llibxsmm_440` traversal, keep the two 32-row halves together, but make the 32-column B/C panel the outer loop and the 64-row A/scratch block the inner loop. Coordinate B and C panel pointers, A row-block offsets, scratch packing lifetime, and the existing 512-step reductions; retain the full512 fallback for other sizes. This tests whether reuse of the current B panel across more output rows improves locality. It is unmeasured advice and does not predict a gain.", "risks": "The current assembly couples pointer resets and advancement to its original nesting, so an incomplete reorder can duplicate or omit output elements, read the wrong B/C panel, or consume stale packed A. The packed A panel must remain valid for every inner block that uses it. All calls, packing, and SME transitions remain timed. A full source review and evaluator correctness checks must cover n=512, general sizes and tails, n<=0, output overwrite, the 0.002 tolerance, fixed flags, and single-thread execution. Then use fresh paired controls with unchanged source power mode/settings and report score spread; do not infer causality from noisy scores or attribute joint outcomes to this role."}, "experiment_id": "loop_order", "status": "proposed", "source_hash": "7562203ea8753326f7d10004d50674912e8791c7f78ed90798d8c9e0a468ba0b"}]
